2. Container image components (Gateway deployment)
--------------------------------------------------

The Gateway deployment runs two digest-pinned images. Both are unmodified
upstream images; the full per-package inventory and licence set for each is
enumerated in the Syft SPDX SBOM generated for every release by
`scripts/release/supply-chain-artifacts.sh`, which is the authoritative
component list for a given release.

  caddy:2.11.4-alpine@sha256:5f5c8640...
    Licence: Apache-2.0
    Role: public TLS edge, On-Demand TLS authority enforcement, reverse proxy to
          the Gateway (see deploy/gateway/README.md).

  alpine:3.24.1@sha256:28bd5fe8...
    Licence: the Alpine base image redistributes multiple components under their
      own licences; the notable ones are musl libc (MIT) and BusyBox
      (GPL-2.0-only). The image additionally installs (see
      deploy/gateway/Dockerfile) ca-certificates, curl and
      libcrypto3/libssl3/openssl (Apache-2.0).
    Role: runtime base for the Gateway image.

  golang:1.27.0-alpine3.24@sha256:4c9fe601...
    Licence: build-only. The Go toolchain and Alpine components as above.
    Role: build stage; no part of it is copied into the runtime image except the
          statically built Gateway binary.

Image-level licence review before distributing a Gateway image must be done
against that image's SBOM, not against this summary: the summary lists what this
repository deliberately selects, while the SBOM lists everything an image
actually contains.


3. Build and CI tooling (not redistributed)
-------------------------------------------

These run in CI or at build time and are not shipped inside any release
artifact: GitHub Actions (pinned by commit SHA), Syft and Trivy (digest-pinned
images used to produce SBOMs and vulnerability scans), Gitleaks, Semgrep,
govulncheck, goimports, and `github.com/akavel/rsrc` (Windows resource compiler
used to build the tray icon/manifest resources). Their licence terms apply to
their own use; none of their code is linked into the Agent, the Gateway or the
installers.
